+	// the entry on EVERY process (create() overwrites the map slot), so an
+	// existing active/completed session had started_at reset to now and
+	// turn_count reset to 1 on each new user message — contradicting the
+	// documented status machine
+	// (docs/verification/gap-051-session-status-machine.md), where started_at
+	// is fixed at creation and turn_count only grows. Now create() runs only
+	// for genuinely new sessions; an existing non-cancelled session keeps its
+	// lifecycle and gets only the LastActive/TurnCount bump via update().
+	// GAP-028: cancelled is terminal — a late POST /v1/process for an
+	// already-cancelled session must not resurrect the entry or increment
+	// turn_count. Harness callbacks still run (permissive).
+	// GAP-043: the branch decision reads through snapshot(); the mutation goes
+	// through update() under the store write lock — never a raw *sessionEntry
+	// from get().
